{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T05:13:22.718Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1704"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1704: secret guard flags short credential values only under password keys; api_key, client_secret, token and *_TOKEN/*_SECRET keys pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1704 (filed 2026-11-11). On 2026.11.11 the secret guard flags a short credential value under password and passphrase keys only. A 17-character random value under api_key, client_secret, token, passwd, db_password, private_key, GITHUB_TOKEN, NPM_TOKEN or AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY passes scanMutationSecrets and the default advise write path in the key: v, key=v and JSON spellings. The high_entropy_assignment rule covers token, secret, password, passwd and api_key only from 24 characters with entropy 3.5, and covers neither client_secret nor compound keys such as db_password. Agents paste env excerpts, CI logs and pasted configs into comments and descriptions, and that is exactly the shape that leaks. Packages cannot rely on the SDK scanner, so pm-memory keeps its own parser. Proposal from the issue: one credential-key rule that reuses the pm-gh1699 KEY plus VALUE composition, the structured JSON, Python-dict and XML pass, an 8-character minimum, whitespace-free values and the placeholder exclusions, with a must-allow corpus (token_budget, max_tokens, token_count, placeholders, prose, localization labels)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1704","sdk","secret-guard","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:22.718Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T05:13:22.718Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"One credential-key rule flags 8+ character whitespace-free non-placeholder values under secret, token, api key, private key, access key, client secret, passwd, pwd and compound *_password/*_secret/*_token/*_api_key/*_private_key keys in any case, in key: v, key=v, JSON, Python-dict and XML spellings; A must-allow corpus stays clean: token_budget, max_tokens, output_token_budget, numeric token counts, placeholders, prose and localization labels; The SDK scanMutationSecrets and the CLI advise path agree on the corpus"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A credential value under any common credential key name raises secret_guard_detected"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Only password and passphrase keys flag a 17-character value"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1699","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-12T05:13:22.718Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"42b103b7cd8968f459f01743d0901c11e64cd4d4fb6122c91d851fd6f87ffe0d","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model"